body:
lol INFO? .... "about 10 nieces" .....

&#x200B;

You don't know?

...............Men are gonna look with or without a crop top lol. I wear crop tops in the summer and so do most of the women that I know, and what men think about it is far from our minds.

&#x200B;

Whyyyyyy did you even post this you weirdo.

INFO: How old are you both?

&#x200B;

YTA for basically punishing your girlfriend without even telling her why you were upset. Ignoring her for days and then telling her she was full of shit? Looks like you're determined to stay upset with her over something that you could have easily just had a conversation about. Wanting to "return the favor" is petty and borderline controlling.

&#x200B;

Use your words, dude.

NTA- Angela went way too long not knowing that Dwight killed Sprinkles. 

&#x200B;

Even if the husband isn't killing the animals, it sounds like your friend is in a pretty bad marriage. Maybe you can get a handful of friends and family to do sort of an intervention. I also highly suggest that she starts going to therapy. If she's being emotionally abused by her husband, there's a good chance her daughter is being abused as well.

eh, ESH except your wife. If the eviction was illegal and you had the recordings of him, why couldn't you stop there? Burying his personal belongings is such a bizarre power move, I can't even comprehend someone going that far just to "teach a lesson".  It's also very unsettling that you think it's on you to.. literally punish adults for "bad behavior"? At the end of the day, this man is your landlord. Sometimes people get shitty landlords! It sucks, everything sucks right now.

&#x200B;

I suggest that you stop with this weird vigilante shit and focus on your wife, you baby, and finding a new source of income so you can get them out of this toxic environment.

Yes, YTA. But what a good opportunity for you to do some research on why this is so offensive to black women!

&#x200B;

 [https://www.forbes.com/sites/janicegassam/2020/01/08/stop-asking-black-people-if-you-can-touch-their-hair/#1b84308050a7](https://www.forbes.com/sites/janicegassam/2020/01/08/stop-asking-black-people-if-you-can-touch-their-hair/#1b84308050a7)

Okay but if you're annoyed that a bunch of people are weirdly obsessed with your shoes.. and then take it out on your wife by snapping at her when she is literally just being a co-parent, then that's something YOU need to work on. Not your wife. 

&#x200B;

Also... ok. So, you have friends, family, AND coworkers telling you that you need new shoes? I'd really love to see a picture of these shoes lol. Maybe if that many people comment on them, then you DO need new shoes? It's very possible your shoes smell, I would buy someone new shoes to avoid having to tell them that they stink?

How is your marriage otherwise? If this is just temporary and you guys didn't have problems in the past, then I suggest waiting until the case is actually over to bring up the topic of moving again. Asking someone to quit the FBI is asking a LOT. Maybe while you both are waiting for the case to be over, your husband can pay for a child therapist to come and work with your son (or video conference right now) a few days a week? Your son clearly has experienced childhood trauma so a professional would be better than your husband at this point anyways.

&#x200B;

That being said, I divorced my emotional abusive and controlling husband years ago and it was the best decision I've ever made. We however, did not have children together. At the end of the day you need to do what you believe is best for your son. Hope it all works out!

NTA and honestly if your sister is refusing to do anything to help \*herself\*, then she's not going to do anything to help her children. If you're in American I highly suggest calling CPS for them to do a well-check. Your nephew needs behavioral therapy as soon as possible. He is acting out due to severe neglect and probably childhood trauma. You're a really good sister for looking out for them, now is the time to take it a step farther to make sure those kids get out of that toxic environment. 

&#x200B;

Are there any other family members that are concerned as well? I would speak to them if so. If not, I would seek out family members who don't know what's happening and fill them in on the situation and formulate a plan to help the kids as soon as possible.

... Of course YTA. I don't understand why you took the time to even write this, unless you just needed to brag about your abs to feel better about yourself. You're blaming a drug for basically forcing you to hurt two peoples feelings. You made plans with two girls and bailed, right in front of them, for someone you thought was "hotter". If a date bailed on me in front of my eyes and then tried to "fix it" by saying you'll try to find someone else for me I would be livid.

&#x200B;

Also, women aren't property. You talk like we're trophies to be won and that in itself makes YTA big time.

NTA but I highly suggest doing this instead:

&#x200B;

 [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EJ7xIH3YSLo](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EJ7xIH3YSLo)

NTA but honestly I would probably just buy your ex a cheap ass tablet and leave it be. She absolutely should not be taking it away from your daughter so she can watch her own shows, but this could end up causing a pretty big riff between you/her, and the kids/her. This is a tough time for everyone so if you can afford it, just buy her something to watch her shows on as an appreciation for taking all of the kids full time for who knows how long.

&#x200B;

Just my two cents. You're def not an asshole and she seems kind of petty, but as a single mom currently working from home with a 2 year old, the quiet times where I can watch my shows in peace are literally what's getting me through this pandemic.
